            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0566" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2293: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Poindexter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-15T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>50. Your No. 58, May 14, 9 a.m. This morning I called in Ambassador Velarde, who
                    said he had not yet received instructions. In your interview with President
                    Leguía did he confirm my understanding of his proposal as I set it forth in my
                    No. 49, May 12, 2 p.m.? Did President explain what disposition is thought of for
                    city of Arica? <pb facs="0567" n="435" xml:id="pg435"/> I do not understand what
                    he means by formula of negotiation: “Peru ratifies promise made to Bolivia to
                    grant her in the plebiscitary territory a corridor to the sea.” Please cable
                    reply as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
